MID_SE_Naz_Dai_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_C_001: Alright, that's it. Enough is enough!
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_C_002: Keep it down... The fish is gonna get away...
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_C_003: That's enough with the nonsense jabbering too.\nGet. UP!
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_C_004: OW, what the heck? I was sleeping, man!
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_C_005: Can it. You're on cleaning duty today. This is the\ntenth time I've covered for you!
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_C_006: They're letting us stay here for cheap as long as we\ntake care of business, so stop slacking!
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_C_007: Eh, who cares. I'm better in combat than you, so I\ndon't need to do stupid things like "cleaning."
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_C_008: Hang on, what? Everyone knows you're weaker than\nme. Again with the nonsense.
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_C_009: Allow me to demonstrate my superior strength.
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_C_010: Let go! Put me down!
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_C_011: Let go, eh? No prob! Hrah!
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_C_012: Mr. Nezha, I'm glad you're so fast at cleaning, but\nyou need to— Agh!
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_C_013: Why do I have to be the one to go buy food?
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_C_014: It's because your cleaning's sloppy. They yelled at me\nfor your bad job. I should be the one who's annoyed.
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_C_015: What'd you say? It was your turn to clean anyway!
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_C_016: If you hadn't thrown me at the innkeeper, he\nwouldn't have gotten so mad at us!
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_C_017: You're blaming me for this? It's clearly your fault\nthat we're out here!
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_C_018: Ugh, you always make things harder than they need\nto be.
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_C_019: Gimme that wallet. I'll hang on to it.
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_C_020: No way. Trying to act all superior, but you're the one\nwho keeps making a mess of things.
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_C_021: I'm the oldest here, so I'll manage the money.
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_C_022: Pfft, as if age matters to me. I was constructed—\nI'm ageless!
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_C_023: I'll pry it outta your grubby hands. Hyah!
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_C_024: Think you can take me down with a weak punch like\nthat?! Ha! Hrah!
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_C_025: Whew... Give up already, will ya? Ugh.\nSo annoying...
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_C_026: Haaah... Haaah... So are you! Agh!
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_C_027: Yikes, you two look rough. Do you need some\nmedicine? I'll sell it to you at a discount!
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_C_028: I can't stop thinking about dinner. Let's head back.
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_C_029: Hey, uh, Dadao? Why did we come to town again?
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_C_030: To fight, obviously. Wait... No, that wasn't it. I, uh,\nforgot...
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_C_031: Agh! Damn it! I forgot to buy the stuff we came here\nfor, and now we're out of money!
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_C_032: I am not taking responsibility! This is all on you!
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_B_001: Alright. It's time. Time to settle things once and\nfor all!
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_B_002: Maybe the innkeeper forgave us, but I haven't\nforgiven you for being such a pain.
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_B_003: Hey, that's my line! Anyway, he only let us off\nbecause I apologized profusely.
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_B_004: So how do you wanna settle it? Up till now, we've\nonly ever had draws.
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_B_005: If we do an eating contest, we'll run out of money\nbefore it's over...
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_B_006: In that strength competition, we got so noisy that a\nbaby started wailing and we had to stop...
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_B_007: Yeah, so I've got a better idea. This board game is\nsuper popular right now.
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_B_008: A battle of wits, huh? Fine by me. There's no way\nI'm dumber than you.
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_B_009: Hmmm... Take that!
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_B_010: Aah! You are...so incredibly stupid. What were you\nthinking with a move like that? Here.
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_B_011: I...lost?! Ugh! How did you do that?!
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_B_012: Well, whatever. Don't let it go to your head. I've got\nthe next challenge. I'll show you true intelligence!
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_B_013: Last question: Dagda the Great sent several\nexpeditions to the forbidden land, but...
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_B_014: I know! Only once! The remaining four were all sent\nby his son Solel!
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_B_015: Ah, you answered everything correctly! What a\nstudious young man you are. With that, I'll be off.
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_B_016: Ha! Proof that you're stupid, and I'm smarter\nthan you!
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_B_017: Argh, you're so obnoxious! And who was that old\nguy, anyway?
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_B_018: I don't know. A scholar, I think? He likes teaching\nkids about history.
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_B_019: Who cares about the past, anyway? Besides, don't\nyou hate lectures?
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_B_020: I mean, yeah. All that info was already programmed\ninto me when I was made. I just don't use it much.
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_B_021: So you didn't even have to study or learn anything?\nDon't be so proud—that's cheating!
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_B_022: Pfft, shut your trap! I won fair and square! But...I\nguess I lost before that...
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_B_023: Yeah, which means it's still a draw. But I'm not\nconvinced you and I are equals.
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_B_024: That's what I was gonna say... Hey, why do you\nalways want to prove you're better than me, huh?
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_B_025: Isn't it obvious? If I can beat you, that means I can\nbeat Anatolia, and all the ladies will fawn over me.
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_B_026: That's ridiculous... And anyway, I was only made\nto be strong.
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_B_027: So if I lose to someone like you, there's no point\nin living!
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_B_028: I take offense to that! C'mon, let's go. I'll beat you\ninto dust!
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_B_029: Who do you think you're talking to? Hehe.\nBring it on!
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_A_001: That battle was fantastic. I still can't believe you\nthrew that chariot!
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_A_002: I was shocked by how light it ended up being! But I\nknow the enemy was even more shocked, ha!
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_A_003: Then you pounced on the enemy camp, and victory\nwas immediate!
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_A_004: Hah, the enemies were sooo slow and boring.\nGotta end boring battles quick.
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_A_005: Yeah! Get 'em over with so we can eat some good\nfood. Thanks for knocking 'em out so fast, Nezha!
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_A_006: And you helped by being wildly unpredictable!\nSeems like we get along better these days...
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_A_007: We lean on each other's strengths, and we really\ncomplement one another.
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_A_008: Yeah... After battles, we just eat and sleep, so that\ndoesn't leave much room for fighting each other.
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_A_009: Remember how much trouble we used to get in for\nthat? Things have really changed.
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_A_010: They have. If we defeat our enemies, there'll be\npeace, which means you and I can get back to it!
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_A_011: Then we can finally figure out who's stronger.\nWe left off with a draw before, after all.
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_A_012: Yeah, let's go! Wh— Eh...
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_A_013: Eh? What's wrong?
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_A_014: I dunno... Before, I wanted to beat you so all the\nladies would know I'm superior.
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_A_015: Now I want to beat you so that you'll acknowledge\nme, because you're super strong and awesome...
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_A_016: Wait, hang on... But that's what I've been trying to\nget you to do!
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_A_017: You know I want to be the strongest. Why else do\nyou think I've been challenging you this whole time?
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_A_018: Hahaha. Then once things die down enough, let's\nfight each other to see who's acknowledged first!
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_A_019: Yeah! I'll definitely beat you, so you better not die\nanytime soon!
MID_SE_Naz_Dai_A_020: Same to you! If you die, I'll punch you!